The exact npm match does not establish the complete build-input ancestry or
all redistribution obligations. See the unresolved findings in the inventory.

Development and external tools (not shipped with the app)
---------------------------------------------------------

* Playwright and Playwright Core 1.65.1: locked Apache-2.0 dev dependencies;
  upstream LICENSE, NOTICE and ThirdPartyNotices are retained separately.
  Browser downloads are test tools, not covered by a blanket Apache claim.
* TypeScript 5.9.3: local Apache-2.0 comparator parser only; its exact parser
  file matched official npm bytes. It is not a project or runtime dependency.
  This is distinct from the tslib helpers embedded in pdf-lib.
* qpdf 12.4.2 and Poppler 25.04.0: separately installed, nonredistributed CLI
  test oracles. qpdf reports Apache-2.0; Poppler is GPL with GPLv2 text in its
  distribution. Neither is bundled into the app. This is not an audit of their
  linked dependencies, upstream license variants or downstream binaries.

See docs/licenses/README.md for verification and update instructions. The
plan permits MIT and specified permissive licenses with their notices; that
permission does not clear these inherited GPL or unverified components.
